From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32, comctl32, shlwapi: Windows' ordinals are not Wine's named exports

---
diff --git a/dlls/comctl32/comctl32.spec b/dlls/comctl32/comctl32.spec
index 3c5d485..5723d26 100644
--- a/dlls/comctl32/comctl32.spec
+++ b/dlls/comctl32/comctl32.spec
@@ -199,3 +199,15 @@
 @ stdcall RegisterClassNameW(wstr)
 @ stdcall UninitializeFlatSB(long)
 @ stdcall _TrackMouseEvent(ptr)
+
+# Stained Glass OS 7705: Windows' ordinals that Wine left to winebuild's numbering of its named
+# exports (numbers and names from Geoff Chappell's public list of COMCTL32 functions): programs that
+# import them by ordinal got whatever named function was numbered there. Each is declared now: a
+# function Wine has under that name takes the number, the rest are stubs.
+18 stub -noname CreateCheckBoxImageList
+165 stub -noname DestroyPropsheetPageArray
+174 stub -noname CreateDUIPropertySheetPage
+391 stub -noname GetTitleFromPropSheetHeader
+392 stub -noname PremultiplyAlphaChannel
+393 stub -noname CreateSmallerIcon
+395 stub -noname Markup_Create
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shell32.spec b/dlls/shell32/shell32.spec
index c51ed85..049a5c0 100644
--- a/dlls/shell32/shell32.spec
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shell32.spec
@@ -220,8 +220,10 @@
  506 stdcall SHRegOpenKeyA (long str long)
  507 stdcall SHRegOpenKeyW (long wstr long)
  508 stdcall SHRegQueryValueA(long str ptr ptr)
- 509 stdcall SHRegQueryValueExA(long str ptr ptr ptr ptr)
- 510 stdcall SHRegQueryValueW (long long long long)
+# Stained Glass OS 7705: 509 is SHRegQueryValueW and 510 SHRegQueryValueExA (A, W, ExA, ExW, as
+# Geoff Chappell's public list numbers them); Wine had the two swapped.
+ 509 stdcall SHRegQueryValueW (long long long long)
+ 510 stdcall SHRegQueryValueExA(long str ptr ptr ptr ptr)
  511 stdcall SHRegQueryValueExW (long wstr ptr ptr ptr ptr)
  512 stdcall SHRegDeleteKeyW (long wstr)
 
@@ -419,7 +421,7 @@
 @ stdcall SHIsFileAvailableOffline(wstr ptr)
